<title>JAPAN: Hokkaido Takushoku up sharply on merger.</title>
<headline>Hokkaido Takushoku up sharply on merger.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hokkaido Takushoku Bank Ltd shares rose sharply after being bid-only on Wednesday morning, buoyed by the bank's planned merger with Hokkaido Bank Ltd in April 1998.</p>
<p>Trading of shares in both banks was suspended for the whole session on Tuesday.</p>
<p>At 0125 GMT, Hokkaido Takushoku shares stood at 170 yen after closing at 153 yen on Monday. Its trading volume of 6.367 million shares was the second heaviest on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange. Hokkaido Bank stood at 170 yen after finishing at 163 on Monday.</p>
</text>
